@startuml Maintenance-SD-ReadModelQuery
autonumber
title Query side — any replica answers alone, even with the owner down (US116, US218, US219, GET by id)
actor "Maintenance\nSupervisor" as User
participant "maintenance-1\n: MaintenanceRecordController" as Ctrl
participant ": ViewMaintenanceRecordsService" as Svc
participant "REPLICATED_MAINTENANCE_RECORD\n(H2 file of replica 1)" as RM
participant "maintenance-2\n(owner of some records, DOWN)" as M2 #LightGray

activate User
User -> Ctrl : GET /api/maintenance-records/ongoing?page=0&size=20
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Svc : ongoing(0, 20)
activate Svc
Svc -> RM : findAll() + RecordFilter(status = IN_PROGRESS)
RM --> Svc : rows of replicas 1, 2 and 3
Svc -> Svc : sort (most recent first), cut the page
Svc --> Ctrl : PageDTO<MaintenanceRecordDTO> (ownerInstance per record)
deactivate Svc
Ctrl --> User : 200 OK (no X-Partial-Response)
deactivate Ctrl

User -> Ctrl : GET /api/maintenance-records/{id of a record owned by replica 2}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Svc : getById(id)
Svc -> RM : findById(id)
RM --> Svc : row (ownerInstance = maintenance-2)
Ctrl --> User : 200 OK
deactivate Ctrl

User -> Ctrl : PATCH /api/maintenance-records/{same id}/component
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> M2 : forwardToOwner (X-Peer-Hops: 1, X-Service-Key)
M2 --> Ctrl : connection refused (retry, circuit breaker)
Ctrl --> User : 503 Service Unavailable (only the owner may change the record)
deactivate Ctrl
deactivate User

note over User, M2
  Assignment 1: the same GET asked the peers over HTTP; a stopped replica made its records invisible (404)
  and lists partial (X-Partial-Response: true). Assignment 2: no peer call on reads.
end note
@enduml
